questions.explanation:
**Given:**

In &Delta;PMN, &ang;P = 76&deg;

Bisectors of the exterior angles at M and N intersect at O

**Formula used:**

Exterior angle bisectors of a triangle intersect at 90&deg; - (&ang;P/2)

Where &ang;P is third angle of the triangle.

**Calculation:**

&ang;P = 76&deg;

&rArr; &ang;MON = 90&deg; - (&ang;P/2)

&rArr; &ang;MON = 90&deg; - (76&deg;/2)

&rArr; &ang;MON = 90&deg; - 38&deg;

&rArr; &ang;MON = 52&deg;

**Hence, the correct answer is option (2).**

